.Dd March 31, 2025
.Dt PATH_ABSOLUTE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm path_absolute ,
.Nm path_absolute_s
.Nd convert a path to an absolute path
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In path.h
.Ft int
.Fn path_absolute "const char *path" "stralloc *sa"
.Ft char *
.Fn path_absolute_s "const char *path"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn path_absolute
function converts the relative or absolute pathname
.Fa path
into an absolute pathname and stores the result in
.Fa sa .
.Pp
The
.Fn path_absolute_s
function performs the same conversion and returns a newly allocated null-terminated string containing the absolute path.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn path_absolute
returns 1 if the path was relative and converted, or 0 if it was already absolute.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr path_absolute_sa 3 ,
.Xr path_is_absolute 3